# Backend Java

## Naming

- Packages: `com.ailab.<feature>`
- Classes: `CourseController`, `CourseService`, `ChunkRepository`
- Nested request DTOs: `public record CreateCourseRequest(...)` inside the controller
- Row DTOs: `public record CourseRow(...)` inside the repository
- IDs: `String` UUID via `UUID.randomUUID().toString()`
- Timestamps: ISO-8601 `Instant.now().toString()` stored as TEXT

## Patterns (do this)

1. Constructor injection, final fields, `@Service` / `@Repository` / `@RestController`
2. Validate inputs in service; Russian messages (`"title ╨╛╨▒╤П╨╖╨░╤В╨╡╨╗╨╡╨╜"`)
3. SQL only in repositories, parameterized (`?`), text blocks for multi-line SQL
4. SQLite nullables: use `toLong(rs.getObject(...))` тАФ never cast `Integer`тЖТ`Long` blindly
5. Course AI routes live on `/api/courses/{courseId}/...` (see `CourseAiController`)

## File template

```java
package com.ailab.feature;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import java.util.Map;

@Service
public class FeatureService {
    private final FeatureRepository repo;
    private final CourseService courses;

    public FeatureService(FeatureRepository repo, CourseService courses) {
        this.repo = repo;
        this.courses = courses;
    }

    public Map<String, Object> doThing(String courseId, String input) {
        courses.requireOwned(courseId);
        if (input == null || input.isBlank()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("input ╨╛╨▒╤П╨╖╨░╤В╨╡╨╗╨╡╨╜");
        }
        // ...
        return Map.of("status", "ok");
    }
}
```

## Antipatterns (forbidden)

- тЭМ Field/`@Autowired` injection
- тЭМ Raw concatenated SQL or SQL in controllers
- тЭМ Swallowing exceptions / empty catch
- тЭМ Returning entities with snake_case JSON keys
- тЭМ Skipping `requireOwned` on course-scoped endpoints
- тЭМ Committing `application-local.yml` or hardcoding API keys
